From be5a8ca8313f091e2d8b3b81c196b42e1a79cd13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:10:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Keep the fallen in the player's Registry

A dead investigator retired by its replacement, or left with a retired
campaign, vanished from the player's Registry (issue #47). A Fallen
section at the Registry's foot now lists each one with its name, its
campaign and an ink Fallen stamp, with no Play, Leave or Delete. A dead
investigator not yet replaced stays under In a campaign. DESIGN.md,
FAQ.md and QUIRKS.md describe it.

Checked in Chromium at 390x844, 820x1180 and 1366x768 for a replaced
investigator, and at 390x844 and 1366x768 for one left with a retired
campaign: the section is last, lists name and campaign, holds no
controls, and the page logs no errors. Frontend builds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WaLz6UBTQ5XaTKSYwqeMKA
